From 645f4c8eb0d2a9d6886d9f69e24466044fae9881 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 15:54:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 242/638] devtools: depend on enterprise buildflags directly
 [chromium] [build]

AI_PHASE: chromium-phase-4-ozone

AI_STATUS: build-validated

ROOT_CAUSE: devtools_window.cc includes file_select_helper.h, which directly includes the generated enterprise buildflags header. The devtools target intentionally cannot depend on //chrome/browser:browser because of a GN cycle, so a regenerated MessageCenter graph compiled devtools before that browser-owned header existed.

FIX_REASON: Add the enterprise buildflags generator beside the target's existing explicit indirect dependencies for the same browser-cycle constraint.

SCOPE: chrome/browser/devtools/BUILD.gn only.

VALIDATION: ninja -C out/aros-windowed chrome -j48 regenerated the graph, compiled all 5980 object/archive steps, and linked the 69,696,356,792-byte unmerged Chrome ET_REL successfully.

RISK: This adds only build ordering and generated-header availability; compile-time enterprise feature values and runtime behavior are unchanged.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap;; MessageCenter graph regeneration -> missing components/enterprise/buildflags/buildflags.h -> direct generator dependency.
---
 chrome/browser/devtools/BUILD.gn | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/devtools/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/devtools/BUILD.gn
index bf03e44832..a85a30f4ee 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/devtools/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/devtools/BUILD.gn
@@ -113,6 +113,7 @@ static_library("devtools") {
     "//chrome/browser/autofill:autofill",
     "//components/autofill/content/browser:browser",
     "//components/autofill/core/browser:browser",
+    "//components/enterprise/buildflags",
     "//components/paint_preview/buildflags:buildflags",
     "//content/public/browser",
     "//net",
